# MediaServo production .env template
#
# Copy to .env and fill, then: docker compose --env-file .env up -d
# .env is gitignored (carries secrets); this template is tracked.
# The compose `${VAR:?}` floor fails fast on an empty required var.

# --- contract: four required vars (all pass-through to the container) ---

# Image tag pin (rollback = re-pin the previous tag and `up -d` again).
TAG=0.1.3

# Site-reachable SFU announced IP. MULTI-NIC SITES MUST EXPLICIT-FILL the IP that
# clients reach (public/LAN). Auto-detect is dev-only: it concatenates all NIC
# IPs but the SFU takes the first only = silent ICE failure.
MEDIASERVO_SFU_ANNOUNCED_IP=

# First-boot admin password (init bootstrap account; persisted in the etc volume;
# rotate afterwards via the admin API). Required — empty fails fast.
MEDIASERVO_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Host ssh maintenance port (container 22 standard; host 2222 default avoids the
# host sshd conflict). Key-only auth; deliver authorized_keys into the
# etc volume (see the site runbook).
SSH_PORT=2222

# --- optional: pin the signaling PSK (recommended for host/vehicle fleets) ---
# First-boot-only bootstrap: a non-empty valid value ([A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,256},
# e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) is written into etc/server.yaml instead of a
# random one; an INVALID value REFUSES TO START (fail-fast: container Exited,
# init error in the logs). Existing volumes are never rotated (change = admin API or a
# `down -v` rebuild). Pinning keeps client apps working across volume loss /
# host migration. KEEP this line after handover (it is the recovery seed);
# store .env securely (chmod 600).
#MEDIASERVO_PSK=

# --- optional tuning (defaults shown; uncomment to override) ---

# Brand — defaults mediaservo, matching the mediaservo-branded image AND the interpolated
# volume paths. Override only for a standalone mediaservo image+compose pair.
#MEDIASERVO_BRAND=mediaservo

# Container memory limit (memory only; CPU unset for RTP bursts).
# Recommended ladder:
#   512m  standard tier — 10 rooms / 20 peers @720p (MEASURED peak 56.81 MiB, ~9x headroom)
#   1g    ~2x standard — e.g. 20 rooms / 40 peers (extrapolated; verify on site)
#   2g    ~4x standard — e.g. 50 rooms / 100 peers (extrapolated; re-measure before relying on it)
# Memory scales with the room/peer object graph, not bitrate; re-measure when
# doubling the tier.
#MEM_LIMIT=512m